{"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1OTY3ODc0","is_bot":false,"login":"stardeltapower","name":""},"baseRefOid":"be6b67a8562a448d538f385a43c46718956cbc31","body":"## What this adds\n\nTwo related additions to the IEC 60909 zero-sequence / single-phase (`fault=\"1ph\"`) short-circuit model, motivated by earth-fault studies on systems earthed through a neutral earthing resistor (NER) and/or a zigzag earthing transformer:\n\n**1. Neutral earthing impedance for ordinary transformers (`rn_ohm`).**\n`xn_ohm` already exists but is only applied to power-station-unit transformers, and only as a reactance. This PR adds `rn_ohm` (resistive part) to `create_transformer` / `create_transformer_from_parameters` (and the bulk variants) and applies the neutral earthing impedance `3·(rn_ohm + j·xn_ohm)` to the zero-sequence impedance of **all** earthed-star vector groups (`dyn`, `ynd`, `yyn`, `ynyn`, `yny`, `yzn`), referred via the earthed-winding bus voltage and applied after the IEC transformer correction factor (the NER is not part of the transformer impedance). This lets a neutral earthing resistor limit the single-phase earth-fault current, as it physically does.\n\n**2. Zigzag earthing transformer vector groups (`ZNyn`, `ZNd`, `ZNy`, `ZN`).**\nCurrently the zero-sequence model raises for Z-connected transformers. Per the YNzn zero-sequence model, the zigzag winding completely decouples the primary and secondary zero sequences and presents a low-impedance shunt-to-ground at its terminal: the HV-winding leakage portion (`si0_hv_partial`) in series with `3·Z_N` at the star point. An earthed-wye secondary (`ZNyn`) gets its own decoupled zero-sequence path (LV leakage portion + zero-sequence magnetising); a delta / unearthed secondary (`ZNd` / `ZNy`) has none. This enables single-phase earth-fault studies on delta-fed networks earthed via a zigzag transformer (common for MV solar/BESS collector systems).\n\n## Tests\n\nAdded to `pandapower/test/shortcircuit/test_1ph.py` (parametrized over both solver paths):\n- `test_trafo_neutral_earthing_impedance` — asserts the neutral earthing impedance adds exactly `3·Z_N` to the zero-sequence Thévenin impedance and leaves the positive sequence unchanged.\n- `test_zigzag_earthing_transformer` — asserts a zigzag earths a delta-fed system, the NER limits the earth fault, and the primary/secondary zero sequences decouple (earthed-wye secondary has an LV path; delta secondary does not).\n\nAll existing `test_1ph` / `test_iec60909_4` tests still pass (the existing power-station-unit `xn_ohm` behaviour is unchanged — `rn_ohm` defaults to `nan`).\n\n## Validation\n\nCross-checked on a real 132/33/0.8 kV solar collector network against DIgSILENT PowerFactory and textbook hand calculations: 3-phase agrees to ~0.5%, and the single-phase earth fault is reproduced (132 kV from the grid zero-sequence, the 33 kV NER-limited fault, and the inverter-LV) within modelling tolerance. The zigzag model follows the same zero-sequence equivalent circuit as the PowerFactory 2-winding transformer technical reference and the J&P Transformer Book.\n\n## Note\n\nCHANGELOG updated. Happy to adjust naming/placement to match maintainer preferences — and to sign the CLA if required.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","commits":[{"authoredDate":"2026-05-31T10:00:47Z","authors":[{"email":"<email>","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1OTY3ODc0","login":"stardeltapower","name":"Ryan Smith"},{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)"}],"committedDate":"2026-05-31T10:00:47Z","messageBody":"…formers in zero-sequence short circuit\n\n- add rn_ohm (resistive neutral earthing) to create_transformer /\n  create_transformer_from_parameters and the bulk variants; apply the neutral\n  earthing impedance 3*(rn_ohm + j*xn_ohm) to the zero-sequence impedance of all\n  earthed-star vector groups, after the IEC transformer correction factor.\n  Previously xn_ohm was only considered for power-station-unit transformers, and\n  only as a reactance, so a neutral earthing resistor (NER/NGR) could not be\n  modelled for ordinary earthed transformers.\n- add zigzag earthing transformer vector groups ZNyn / ZNd / ZNy / ZN. Per the\n  YNzn zero-sequence model the zigzag winding completely decouples the primary\n  and secondary zero sequences and presents a shunt-to-ground: the HV-winding\n  leakage portion (si0_hv_partial) in series with 3*Z_N at the star point. An\n  earthed-wye secondary (ZNyn) gets its own decoupled zero-sequence path to\n  ground (LV leakage portion + zero-sequence magnetising); a delta / unearthed\n  secondary (ZNd / ZNy) has none.\n- add unit tests in test_1ph: neutral earthing adds exactly 3*Z_N to the zero\n  sequence; zigzag earthing of a delta-fed system, with the NER limiting it and\n  the primary/secondary decoupling.\n- update changelog.\n\nEnables IEC 60909 single-phase earth-fault studies on delta-fed systems earthed\nthrough a neutral earthing resistor and/or a zigzag earthing transformer.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","messageHeadline":"[ADDED] neutral earthing impedance (rn_ohm) and zigzag earthing trans…","oid":"eb95238fa1b94275bf4fbcc61d330f554b1c5486"},{"authoredDate":"2026-07-04T09:19:54Z","authors":[{"email":"<email>","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0Mjc4MjA=","login":"vogt31337","name":"Mike Vogt"}],"committedDate":"2026-07-04T09:19:54Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"fixed naming convention issues.","oid":"12a8af8bc53fb50e6211a5c76beda1efdb2b4b74"},{"authoredDate":"2026-07-04T09:23:56Z","authors":[{"email":"<email>","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0Mjc4MjA=","login":"vogt31337","name":"V3"}],"committedDate":"2026-07-04T09:23:56Z","messageBody":"","messageHeadline":"Merge branch 'develop' into feature/trafo-neutral-earthing-zigzag","oid":"9b544669e813e7138560acd9338412c03454cfe9"}],"files":[{"path":"CHANGELOG.rst","additions":3,"deletions":0},{"path":"pandapower/create/trafo_create.py","additi